    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔγραμμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-designed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραφαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Is.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; <i>well-drawn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>; <i>of graceful contour</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ.
				τῇ συστάσει</span>, of a person, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.5.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρύων τὸ εὔ</span>. their
				<i>fine lines</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Im.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμμως</span>,
			of architecture, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mag.</u>
				3.70
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>well-defined</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοδοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> masc.,
				<i>a good writer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				5.245
			</span></i>.</div>
